    "title": "A quantitative Escher height from strictly ascending chains modulo the infimum",
    "description": "Define the Escher height of a commutative ring as the supremum, over all infinite strictly ascending chains of ideals I_0 < I_1 < ... whose infimum equals I_0, of a rank measured by the maximal length of a chain of prime ideals sandwiched strictly between consecutive rungs. The conjecture is that for a polynomial ring k[x_1,...,x_n] over a field every such 'grounded' chain is finite so the height is 0, for k[x_1,x_2,...] in countably many variables the height is infinite, and for the ring of integer-valued polynomials Int(Z) the height equals its Krull dimension 2. Approach: build explicit grounded chains, control the prime sandwiches via going-up/going-down, and separate the finite from the infinite case using the ascending chain condition. The key insight is that the informal 'Krull dimension gap' only becomes a well-defined invariant once you tie each rung of the ascending chain to a prime chain living strictly between it and its successor.",
