    "description": "Extend Escher staircases from ideals to submodules: a module M over R admits an Escher staircase if it has an infinite strictly ascending chain of submodules. Conjecture: a finitely generated module over a commutative ring R admits an Escher staircase iff R itself is non-Noetherian, so the module-level phenomenon is governed entirely by the base ring, whereas for infinitely generated modules the free module R^{(N)} always admits one regardless of R. Approach: reduce the finitely generated case to R via a surjection from a free module and the fact that quotients and submodules of Noetherian modules are Noetherian; construct the free-module staircase from coordinate submodules. The key insight is that finite generation transports the ascending chain condition faithfully between a module and its base ring, pinning the staircase to the ring exactly when the module is finitely generated.",
